{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"total overtime hours per month for the entire workforce cannot exceed 20 hours per worker,\" do you mean each individual worker can work at most 20 overtime hours in a month (so total overtime = 20 × number of workers that month), or that the whole workforce combined can work at most 20 overtime hours in total per month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the interpretation of the overtime limit, presenting two mutually exclusive options for one constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the regular wage, you said it's paid regardless of utilization — does that mean the company pays 1,000 workers × 160 hours × 30 Yuan every month even if they produce nothing, or is the regular wage paid only for the hours actually used (up to 160 per worker)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the calculation basis of the regular wage (fixed monthly amount vs. hours actually used), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say orders are fulfilled using \"available inventory from the previous month, current in-house production, and outsourced units,\" does the fulfillment order matter for cost purposes — that is, must the model use up previous-month inventory first, then in-house production, then outsourcing — or can any combination of the three sources be used in any order as long as the total meets demand?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the order of fulfillment sources is fixed or flexible."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can the workforce (number of workers) change from month to month, meaning the company can hire or fire workers in any of the six months, or is the workforce fixed at 1,000 workers for the entire January–June period?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the workforce size is variable or fixed over the six-month period."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When workers are hired or fired in a given month, are they available for production in that same month (i.e., the workforce level used for that month's production capacity is the level after hiring/firing), or do they only become available starting the next month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the timing of workforce availability relative to hiring/firing events."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the backorder cost of 35 Yuan per unit — is this charged on the total quantity of unfulfilled demand carried over at the end of each month (i.e., the ending backorder level), or is it charged on the flow of units that become backordered during that month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive calculation methods for the backorder cost."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any limit on how many units can be backordered (i.e., can all unmet demand be carried forward indefinitely), or is there a maximum backorder level or a requirement that all backorders must be cleared by a certain month?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding backorder limits or clearance requirements, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
